---
import CaseLayout from '../layouts/CaseLayout.astro';
import CaseHeader from '../components/f/CaseHeader.astro';
import NextStory from '../components/f/NextStory.astro';

const pct = (v: number, of: number) => `${((v / of) * 100).toFixed(3)}%`;

const facts = [
  { k: 'Role', v: 'UX, information architecture' },
  { k: 'Date', v: 'July – December 2021' },
  { k: 'Team', v: 'Camilo Beltrán, development lead\nNatalia Torres, visual design' },
  { k: 'Link', v: 'Aprender Digital', href: 'https://contenidos.colombiaaprende.edu.co' },
];
const overview = [
  { k: 'Challenge', v: 'Create a product model for rural teachers who can’t rely on internet access as a default.' },
  { k: 'Contribution', v: 'UX, information architecture, value-proposition work and prototyping on a short timeline.' },
  { k: 'Research', v: 'Desk research plus interviews with 10 teachers and 5 ICT leaders serving low-connectivity schools.' },
  { k: 'Outcome', v: 'An offline-ready content package model and a simpler publishing workflow.' },
];
const numbers = [
  { v: '7M+', k: 'rural Colombians without internet access in 2020' },
  { v: '47%', k: 'of rural schools with no network at all in 2020' },
  { v: '3', k: 'months from new proposal to a tested MVP' },
];
const prototypes = [
  {
    label: 'Aprender Digital website (prototype in Spanish)',
    src: 'https://www.figma.com/embed?embed_host=share&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.figma.com%2Fproto%2FSRpGGNHHdLTeOvaZIIjZVz%2FAprender-Digital%3Fpage-id%3D0%253A1%26node-id%3D42%253A2211%26viewport%3D241%252C48%252C0.04%26scaling%3Dmin-zoom%26starting-point-node-id%3D42%253A2211',
    href: 'https://www.figma.com/proto/SRpGGNHHdLTeOvaZIIjZVz/Aprender-Digital?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=42%3A2211&scaling=min-zoom&starting-point-node-id=42%3A2211',
  },
  {
    label: 'Offline content package (prototype in Spanish)',
    src: 'https://www.figma.com/embed?embed_host=share&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.figma.com%2Fproto%2F2OZPNtWxdH1iKL6p4GrCO5%2FContenido-offline%3Fpage-id%3D0%253A1%26node-id%3D4%253A2%26viewport%3D241%252C48%252C0.12%26scaling%3Dmin-zoom%26starting-point-node-id%3D4%253A2',
    href: 'https://www.figma.com/proto/2OZPNtWxdH1iKL6p4GrCO5/Contenido-offline?page-id=0%3A1&node-id=4%3A2&scaling=min-zoom&starting-point-node-id=4%3A2',
  },
];
---

<CaseLayout
  title="Bringing learning to rural classrooms — William Montoya"
  description="How do you get educational resources to rural teachers when internet access can’t be assumed?"
  readFull="6 min"
  readTldr="1 min"
>
  <CaseHeader
    lead="Bringing learning to rural classrooms"
    accent="without internet"
    question="How do you get educational resources to rural teachers when internet access can’t be assumed?"
    facts={facts}
    overview={overview}
    readFull="6 min"
    readTldr="1 min"
  />

  <figure class="figure figure--lead wrap" data-reveal>
    <div class="stage" style="aspect-ratio:1296/640">
      <div class="browser" style={`left:${pct(148, 1296)};top:${pct(56, 640)};width:${pct(1000, 1296)}`}>
        <div class="browser__bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <img src="/assets/aprender-digital-version-ligera.webp" width="1400" height="700" alt="Aprender Digital, light version: the landing page that explains how the offline platform works." fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>

  <section class="chapter chapter--section wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-numbers" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-numbers" class="t-h3 split__label">In numbers</h2>
      <div class="columns3 numbers split__body">
        {numbers.map((n) => (
          <div><p class="t-display">{n.v}</p><p class="t-muted">{n.k}</p></div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-background" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-background" class="t-h3 split__label">Background</h2>
      <div class="prose measure split__body">
        <p>Aprender Digital was a spin-off of Colombia Aprende, created to support the educational community with content and guidelines during the COVID-19 lockdown.</p>
        <p>It was a temporary solution while we finished the new <a class="link" href="https://www.colombiaaprende.edu.co" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">colombiaaprende.edu.co</a>. When the new Colombia Aprende launched in October 2020, Aprender Digital became redundant.</p>
        <p>The brand was already known, though, so the Ministry gave us the chance to rethink it around a new value proposition with a single goal: a solution that works for people without an internet connection.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter chapter--tight wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-process" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-process" class="t-h3 split__label">Process</h2>
      <div class="chapter__stack split__body">
        <div class="prose measure" data-depth="full">
          <p>Unlike Colombia Aprende, we had a tight schedule to propose a new value proposition, define the scope, build an MVP and test it with rural teachers.</p>
          <p>We chose Lean UX because of the timeline. Instead of defining requirements meticulously, we started from desk research to frame the problem.</p>
          <p>Figures from the Ministry of Education and the ICT Ministry showed the scale of the gap: a rural child received about half the education of a peer in Bogotá or Medellín.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid2">
          <div><h3 class="t-small t-muted">Problem statement</h3><p class="insight">The lack of access to educational resources is widening the gap between urban and rural Colombia, and hurting the work of rural teachers.</p></div>
          <div><h3 class="t-small t-muted">Hypothesis</h3><p class="insight">If we deliver resources and guidelines consistently, even without internet, rural teachers can prepare their classes better, and education gets better with it.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="figure wrap" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="stage" style="aspect-ratio:1296/600">
      <img class="flat" src="/assets/lean-ux-framework.webp" width="600" height="600" loading="lazy" alt="The Lean UX cycle: think, make, check." style={`left:${pct(398, 1296)};top:${pct(50, 600)};width:${pct(500, 1296)}`} />
    </div>
  </figure>

  <section class="chapter chapter--tight wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-users" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-users" class="t-h3 split__label">Finding the users</h2>
      <div class="prose measure split__body">
        <p>We brought the regional Education Secretariats into the process and built two proto-personas: a rural teacher and an ICT leader within the Secretariat.</p>
        <p>Then we interviewed 10 teachers and 5 ICT leaders to turn those proto-personas into evidence-based personas.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="figure wrap" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="stage" style="aspect-ratio:1296/760">
      <img class="flat" src="/assets/user-persona.webp" width="1100" height="1080" loading="lazy" alt="Persona card for Carmen Gómez, a rural teacher in Colombia: goals, frustrations and context." style={`left:${pct(318, 1296)};top:${pct(48, 760)};width:${pct(680, 1296)}`} />
    </div>
    <figcaption class="t-small">Rural teacher persona (in Spanish)</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="chapter chapter--tight wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-value" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-value" class="t-h3 split__label">Creating value</h2>
      <div class="chapter__stack split__body">
        <p class="measure" data-depth="full">To define the MVP we first set the new value proposition, running the exercise for both personas. The workshop produced the key insight: Secretariats waited two or three weeks to receive the content they requested, and teachers needed them as one clear package, not resources downloaded one by one.</p>
        <p class="t-h2 pull">A curated content package that teachers carry to class as a single file.</p>
        <p class="measure">Aprender Digital became a microsite of curated packages. Secretariats and teachers download a package as a self-contained HTML interface and carry that one file to the computers in rural schools. On our side, no one assembles packages by hand: we publish content as always, and the CMS does the rest.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <figure class="figure wrap" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="stage" style="aspect-ratio:1296/520">
      <img class="flat" src="/assets/value-proposition-canvas.webp" width="1200" height="363" loading="lazy" alt="Value Proposition Canvas from the workshop, for both personas." style={`left:${pct(98, 1296)};top:${pct(96, 520)};width:${pct(1100, 1296)}`} />
    </div>
    <figcaption class="t-small">The Value Proposition Canvas we ran with both personas (in Spanish)</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="chapter chapter--tight wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-testing" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-testing" class="t-h3 split__label">Prototyping and testing</h2>
      <div class="chapter__stack split__body">
        <p class="measure">We built two interfaces: one for the website and one for the offline packages. The first iterated on the previous site; the second was built on Material Design guidelines.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {prototypes.map((p) => (
    <figure class="figure wrap" data-depth="full" data-reveal>
      <div class="proto" data-proto={p.src} data-title={`${p.label} (Figma)`}>
        <div class="proto__inner">
          <p class="t-small t-muted">{p.label}</p>
          <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Load the prototype</button>
          <a class="link t-small" href={p.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open in Figma <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </figure>
  ))}

  <section class="chapter chapter--section wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-results" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-results" class="t-h3 split__label">Results</h2>
      <div class="prose measure split__body">
        <p>We shipped the MVP in three months. Five years later the portal is still live, draws about 1,200 visits a month, and the Ministry keeps adding content to it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter chapter--section wrap" aria-labelledby="ch-lessons" data-reveal>
    <div class="split">
      <h2 id="ch-lessons" class="t-h3 split__label">Lessons</h2>
      <div class="split__body" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--space-10)">
        <div class="prose measure">
          <p>Shipping the first version quickly was the right call. But content design lagged behind product and UX, and the gap showed in the first weeks. A short beta would have closed it sooner.</p>
        </div>
        <p class="t-h2 pull">Content strategy has to run in parallel with design from the first sprint, not after it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextStory current="/aprender-digital" />
</CaseLayout>

<script>
  // Figma embeds load only when asked: keeps the page light.
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-proto]').forEach((box) => {
    box.querySelector('button')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const f = document.createElement('iframe');
      f.src = box.dataset.proto ?? '';
      f.title = box.dataset.title ?? 'Figma prototype';
      f.allowFullscreen = true;
      box.querySelector('.proto__inner')?.remove();
      box.appendChild(f);
    });
  });
</script>
